## Summary

Implemented `crates/application/src/sidecar.rs` (only source file touched; no `Cargo.toml` change needed — `sha2`/`hex`/`tokio` already present).

**Design** — A-02-compliant ports-driven orchestrator. The `sidecar` provider crate already has the §9.6 policy with hardcoded `ed25519_dalek`; this module transcribes the same §9.6 rules over the `ports::signature::SignatureProvider` trait so any signing backend (in-process, HSM, remote) can be injected without rewriting import policy. Provider types never cross the seam — only the local `SidecarArtifact` DTO (primitive fields + `domain::trust::SignatureEnvelope`).

**API surface:**
- `SidecarImporter::classify(&artifact, &index)` — async, returns `ImportOutcome` (`Duplicate`/`Quarantined`/`RequiresConfirmation`/`Accepted`) after running the §9.6 gates in order: idempotency by `artifact_sha256` → `artifact_id` integrity → unsigned-confirmation → signature verify via port (Invalid/UnknownKey/RevokedKey → quarantine; Verified → continue) → object digest verification → per-annotation conflict resolution (`annotation_id + revision` key, with `Noop`/`Create`/`Stale`/`Conflict` outcomes).
- `SidecarImporter::classify_confirmed(...)` — re-runs the pipeline for an unsigned artifact after explicit user confirmation (idempotency, artifact_id and object-digest gates still apply; signature gate skipped).
- `SidecarExporter::sign_export(canonical_unsigned_bytes)` — signs via port under `SIGNATURE_DOMAIN`, returns `SignedExport { artifact_id, signature }` for the caller's codec to finalize.
- `ImportIndex` for idempotency + per-annotation conflict lookup.
- 17 real-fixture tests covering every §9.6 rule and edge case.

**`cargo check -p application` result:** my module produces **zero errors and zero warnings**. The only check failures are missing types in `crates/ports/src/platform.rs` (`PlatformError`, `PowerState`, `NetworkState`, `PlatformCapabilityReport`, `PlatformStorageRoot`) — that's the in-progress P3-04 task; per task instructions I ignored other-crate errors and did not modify `ports`.
